&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager, Kubernetes Observability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a global team of innovators and pioneers dedicated to shaping the future of observability. At New Relic, we build an intelligent platform that empowers companies to thrive in an AI-first world by giving them unparalleled insight into their complex systems. As we continue to expand our global footprint, we&#39;re looking for passionate people to join our mission. If you&#39;re ready to help the world&#39;s best companies optimize their digital applications, we invite you to explore a career with us!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced Engineering Manager with an eagerness for technology, people, project delivery, and process optimization to lead our Kubernetes Observability team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At New Relic, we love making software that improves the lives of people who make software. The Infrastructure product organization drives New Relic’s customer-facing monitoring experiences, and the Kubernetes ecosystem is at the absolute center of this mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, your team develops and maintains the critical Kubernetes integrations that give our customers full, real-time observability into the health and performance of their K8s environments. You will lead a high-performing team of engineers building Go/Python data collectors, highly scalable backend services, intuitive UI dashboards, and AI-driven K8s SRE Agents that autonomously detect and diagnose complex cluster anomalies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a strong technical background in distributed systems and container orchestration, paired with exceptional mentoring skills and a passion for open-source and AI innovation, we would love to hear from you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and Grow:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage, coach, and mentor a committed group of Go and Python engineers, fostering an inclusive culture where they can grow their professional abilities and share code ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support K8s agent for multiple versions of K8s, Openshift, Rancher, Windows, OKE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Technical Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide architectural decision-making around Kubernetes integrations, OpenTelemetry (OTel) semantic conventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver E2E Value:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure the successful planning and execution of software projects, from the low-level instrumentation agents and Helm charts to the backend services and frontend UI components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate Cross-Functionally:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with Product Managers, Designers, and other engineering teams to align on product goals and deliver high-quality software at a regular cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement DevOps methodologies where the team builds, maintains, and supports its own software, including managing second-layer support rotations and incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Source Advocacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Encourage and support team contributions to the Open Source community to solve sophisticated problems and build New Relic&#39;s engineering reputation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role Requires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 8+ years of overall software engineering experience, with a strong background in large-scale distributed systems and high-cardinality data processing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; 2+ years of experience directly managing and scaling engineering teams in a fast-paced, agile environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of Kubernetes architectures and familiarity with scaling applications in complex, multi-cloud containerized environments (EKS, AKS, GKE).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on background with &lt;strong&gt;Go&lt;/strong&gt; and/or &lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt;, Linux systems, and API development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer &amp;amp; Incident Focus:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience handling customer incidents, diving deep into technical implications, and mitigating risks in production environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong analytical skills with an autonomous, creative approach to overcoming technical blockers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points if You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI/Agent Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Background in building or managing AI workflows, LLM orchestration, or Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability Standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep experience with OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, eBPF, or similar telemetry frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;K8s Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience developing Helm charts, Kubernetes Operators, or working with different Unix OSes and Windows nodes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OSS Contributions:&lt;/strong&gt; Upstream contributions to relevant Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF) or open-source infrastructure projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
